  "title": "Retire B154 ollama-on-demand-activation: teacher-distillation lane decommissioned under the native-only direction",
  "summary": "Governor worklist item 7: B154 still registers Ollama as an external service with explicit demand lanes including teacher distillation (live implementation residue: ollama-service.exe, TeacherCollect.cs, --teacher-collect, teacher-distillation.json). The governed direction is native-only: Xingcheng teacher signal comes from the native self-distillation lane and no external model service is a teacher. This amendment retires B154 outright: rule and prohibition are rewritten to retirement language consistent with retired-article convention (C87/C88), and provision_lifecycle_status moves to retired with no successor. Codex-law change only; implementation removal of the Ollama/teacher-collect artifacts follows separately and is never part of this request.",
  "requested_by": "decision-sovereign",
  "origin": "governor worklist item 7 (2026-10-02): codex B154 still registers Ollama teacher distillation while the teacher-distillation lane is decommissioned; related live request xingcheng-native-teacher-self-distillation-20261002 narrows B154 only - this request proposes full article retirement per the native-only direction",
